{
  "id": "nouns-plurals-this-that",
  "level": "a1",
  "area": "First words, first sentences",
  "title": "Nouns: a/an, plurals, this/that/these/those",
  "tagline": "The words for things: a or an, one or many, and pointing at what's near or far.",
  "cefr": "A1",
  "exam": [
    "Reading Part 5 — open cloze (grammar gaps)",
    "Speaking Part 1 — questions about you and your things"
  ],
  "why": "Nouns are the words for everything around you: your pens, your friends, your pets. Get <i>a/an</i> and the plural right, and every sentence is instantly clearer. <i>This, that, these, those</i> are some of the first words you need to point at things and ask <i>What's this?</i>",
  "hook": {
    "text": "At the market in Cusco, Nadia looks at the stalls. \"Is <b>this</b> a llama toy?\" she asks. \"No,\" says the seller, \"<b>that's</b> an alpaca! <b>This</b> one is the llama.\" Nadia laughs: \"I want <b>an</b> alpaca and two small <b>llamas</b>, please!\"",
    "ask": "Find a word with <i>a</i>, a word with <i>an</i>, and a plural noun with <b>-s</b>. Which word points at something far away?"
  },
